cchi, Flan de Huevo Casero, and Cremoso de Manzana. Additionally, it is utilized in the preparation of Galleta Maria, where it adds both flavor and nutritional value. \n\nLECHE is also noted for its low purine content, making it a suitable option for individuals managing uric acid levels. However, it is important to be aware that milk and its derivatives can interfere with the absorption of certain antibiotics, such as tetracyclines. Furthermore, milk is a liquid with a viscosity ranging from 1 to 50 cP, which makes it appropriate for individuals with dysphagia, as it can be consumed safely in various forms. Overall, LECHE is a fundamental ingredient in many recipes and has important dietary implications.\",33\r\n1503,BRÓCOLI CON SALSA AURORA,\"Brócoli con Salsa Aurora is a dish that features broccoli served with a creamy tomato sauce. It is specifically designed to meet hospital dietary requirements and is also part of dysphagia management recipes, making it suitable for individuals with swallowing difficulties. The creamy sauce enhances the flavor of the broccoli while ensuring that the dish remains accessible for those with specific dietary needs.\",7\r\n1464,FLAN DE HUEVO CASERO,\"FLAN DE HUEVO CASERO is a homemade egg flan dessert designed to be suitable for individuals with dysphagia. This dessert is prepared using a recipe that includes key ingredients such as milk and sugar, ensuring it meets the dietary needs of those who may have difficulty swallowing.\",7\r\n1472,ENSALADILLA RUSA,\"A traditional Spanish salad recipe made with potatoes, carrots, tuna, and mayonnaise, suitable for dysphagia patients.\",3\r\n8309,GALLETAS,\"Galletas, commonly known as cookies, are a type of baked good that can vary significantly in their gluten content. While some galletas may be suitable for gluten-free diets, many traditional varieties contain gluten, making them unsuitable for individuals with celiac disease. Galletas are often consumed as a snack, providing enjoyment and