lly designed for individuals with dysphagia, ensuring it is suitable for those who have difficulty swallowing. This dessert is made with a combination of eggs, milk, sugar, and coffee, and is prepared by baking in a water bath. It is typically served with a layer of caramel, enhancing its flavor and presentation.\",5\r\n8310,MERENDA,\"Merienda is a light meal or snack typically consumed in the afternoon. It often includes items such as galletas (cookies) and leche (milk). This tradition emphasizes a casual and enjoyable break during the day, allowing individuals to recharge with simple yet satisfying food options.\",3\r\n1477,MAYONESA,\"Mayonesa, commonly known as mayonnaise, is a condiment made from emulsified egg yolks and oil. It is widely used in various recipes, including the traditional Spanish dish ensaladilla rusa. Depending on the recipe, mayonesa may contain lactose. However, it is important to note that mayonnaise is not permitted in modified diets. In culinary applications, mayonnaise is utilized in recipes such as cold salmon cake, where it contributes creaminess and flavor.\",2\r\n9749,BIZCOCHOS,Bizcochos are baked goods that may include lactose in their ingredients.,1\r\n9747,CEREALES DE DESAYUNO,\"CEREALES DE DESAYUNO, or breakfast cereals, encompass a wide variety of products that can differ significantly in their ingredients and nutritional content. These cereals may vary in gluten content, with some options being suitable for gluten-free diets, catering to individuals with gluten sensitivities or celiac disease. Additionally, CEREALES DE DESAYUNO may contain lactose as an ingredient, which is important for those who are lactose intolerant to consider when selecting their breakfast options. Overall, CEREALES DE DESAYUNO offers diverse choices that can accommodate different dietary needs and preferences.\",1\r\n9744,LACTASAS,Lactasas are commercial preparations that can be added to foods to help increase tolerance to lactose.,1\r\n9743,SUERO LÁCTEO,